  "solution": "The logic followed here is,\n\nLogic: **Third Number = (First Number + Second Number) × 3 - 1**\n\n**(19, 53, 215)**\n\n→ 215 = (19 + 53) × 3 - 1\n\n→ 215 = 72 × 3 - 1\n\n→ 215 = 216 - 1\n\n**(22, 15, 110)**\n\n→ 110 = (22 + 15) × 3 - 1\n\n→ 110 = 37 × 3 - 1\n\n→ 110 = 111 - 1\n\nNow, let's check each option,\n\n**1) (15, 49, 199)**\n\n→ 199 = (15 + 49) × 3 - 1\n\n→ 199 = (64) × 3 - 1\n\n→ 199 ≠ 192 - 1 \n\n**2) (17, 47, 112)**\n\n→ 112 = (17 + 47) × 3 - 1\n\n→ 112 = (64) × 3 - 1\n\n→ 112 ≠ 192 - 1 \n\n**3) (13, 35, 143)**\n\n→ 143 = (13 + 35) × 3 - 1\n\n→ 143 = (48) × 3 - 1\n\n→ 143 = 144 - 1 ⇒ **Satisfies the logic.**\n\n**4) (18, 50, 230)**\n\n→ 230 = (18 + 50) × 3 - 1\n\n→ 230 = (68) × 3 - 1\n\n→ 230 ≠ 204 - 1 \n\nHere, we can see that only Option 3 satisfies the logic. \n\nHence, the correct answer is **\"(13, 35, 143)\"**.",
